-- title:
--   Nonzero plane relation between s_l/sᵢ and a function h
-- statement:
--   Fix $N \geq 1$ and write $F =$ `modularFunctionFieldBar N` for the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-subfield of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}((t))$ generated over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ by the coefficientwise images of the field `modularFunctionFieldFull N` $\subseteq \mathbb{Q}((t))$, the latter being the $\mathbb{Q}$-subfield of $\mathbb{Q}((t))$ generated by the expansions `divisorExpansions N`. Let $r \in \mathbb{N}$ and let $s : \mathrm{Fin}\,r \to F$ satisfy `IsEmbBasis N s`, i.e. the family $s$ is linearly independent over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ and its $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-span is the Riemann–Roch space $\{f \in F : v(f) \leq \exp(D(v))$ for all places $v$ of $F/\overline{\mathbb{Q}}\}$ attached to the divisor $D =$ `embDivisor N` $= (\,$`embDegree N`$\,)\cdot$`cuspInftyBar N`. Let $h \in F$ be nonzero and let $i, l \in \mathrm{Fin}\,r$. Then there is a polynomial $H \in \overline{\mathbb{Q}}[Z][Y]$ such that $H \neq 0$, the constant term of $H$ in $Y$ is a nonzero element of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}[Z]$ (that is, $H(Z,0) \neq 0$), and, after mapping the coefficients of $H$ into $F$, substituting $Z \mapsto s_l \cdot s_i^{-1}$ and $Y \mapsto h$ gives $0$ in $F$.
--
--   This is the algebraic-dependence input for the value-to-fibre step on $X_0(N)$: a fixed nonzero function $h$ and the ratio $s_l/s_i$ of two coordinate functions satisfy a nonzero plane relation whose specialisation at $h = 0$ is not identically zero, so that smallness of $|h|$ at a point constrains the value of $s_l/s_i$ there. It is used in [`ModularCurve.exists_log_absValue_evalAt_ge_of_forall_prox_le`](thm.html#ModularCurve.exists_log_absValue_evalAt_ge_of_forall_prox_le).
